00:21:58,110 --> 00:22:02,790
but you don't want to sound arrogant. You want to be professional, but not robotic.

449
00:22:02,790 --> 00:22:07,350
That balance can be tricky. It can. But the good news is that introducing yourself in

450
00:22:07,350 --> 00:22:12,790
a business meeting follows a simple structure. I love structure. Structure makes everything

451
00:22:12,790 --> 00:22:19,270
easier. Exactly. A clear introduction usually includes five elements, greeting, name,

452
00:22:19,270 --> 00:22:25,610
position, responsibility, and a brief positive statement, let's break that down slowly.

453
00:22:25,610 --> 00:22:26,610
First the greeting.

454
00:22:26,610 --> 00:22:31,550
Yes, always start with something polite and appropriate to the time of day, for example

455
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:34,590
good morning everyone or good afternoon.

456
00:22:34,590 --> 00:22:39,470
And if it's a virtual meeting, you can say hi everyone, which sounds slightly less formal

457
00:22:39,470 --> 00:22:41,270
but still professional.

458
00:22:41,270 --> 00:22:43,350
After the greeting comes your name.

459
00:22:43,350 --> 00:22:48,510
Right, in formal situations it's better to say my name is instead of just saying

460
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:49,870
your first name.

461
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:54,830
So instead of I'm John, you would say, my name is John Smith.

462
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:55,830
Exactly.

463
00:22:55,830 --> 00:23:00,710
Using your full name adds professionalism, especially when meeting new clients or senior

464
00:23:00,710 --> 00:23:01,710
leaders.

465
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:03,110
Then comes your position.

466
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:05,810
Yes, clearly state your job title.

467
00:23:05,810 --> 00:23:10,870
For example, I'm the marketing manager, or I work as a financial analyst.

468
00:23:10,870 --> 00:23:13,670
Why is mentioning your title so important?

469
00:23:13,670 --> 00:23:18,150
Because it provides context, people immediately understand your role and your level of

470
00:23:18,150 --> 00:23:24,150
responsibility. That makes sense. And then responsibility? Yes, briefly mention what you

471
00:23:24,150 --> 00:23:30,790
actually do. For example, I oversee client accounts in the European market, or I'm responsible

472
00:23:30,790 --> 00:23:35,070
for product development and strategy. That sounds much stronger than just saying your

473
00:23:35,070 --> 00:23:40,630
job title. Exactly. It gives substance to your introduction. And finally, the positive

474
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:45,750
statement. Yes, something like I'm looking forward to working with all of you, or

475
00:23:45,750 --> 00:23:48,470
I'm excited to collaborate on this project.

476
00:23:48,470 --> 00:23:50,390
That leaves a positive impression.

477
00:23:50,390 --> 00:23:51,390
It does.

478
00:23:51,390 --> 00:23:53,670
It shows enthusiasm and openness.

479
00:23:53,670 --> 00:23:56,190
