480
00:23:56,190 --> 00:23:59,150
Sure, here's a model introduction.

481
00:23:59,150 --> 00:24:00,270
Good morning, everyone.

482
00:24:00,270 --> 00:24:04,590
My name is Speaker 2, and I'm the Operations Manager here at the company.

483
00:24:04,590 --> 00:24:08,310
I oversee supply chain coordination and process improvement.

484
00:24:08,310 --> 00:24:12,410
I'm very pleased to be part of this meeting and look forward to working with you.

485
00:24:12,410 --> 00:24:15,710
That sounds confident, structured, and professional.

486
00:24:15,710 --> 00:24:22,910
notice that it's not too long. That's important. Introduction should be concise. Yes, concise means

487
00:24:22,910 --> 00:24:28,830
short, but complete. You don't need to share your entire career history. That's a common mistake.

488
00:24:28,830 --> 00:24:33,790
Some people talk for two or three minutes. Exactly. In most meetings, your introduction

489
00:24:33,790 --> 00:24:39,230
should be between 20 and 40 seconds. Now let's talk about different meeting situations.

490
00:24:39,230 --> 00:24:43,870
Suppose you're the newest member of the team. How would you introduce yourself in your first

491
00:24:43,870 --> 00:24:46,750
internal meeting. In that case, you might say,

492
00:24:46,750 --> 00:24:51,550
Good morning, everyone. My name is Speaker 2, and I've just joined the HR Department

493
00:24:51,550 --> 00:24:56,990
as a talent acquisition specialist. I'll be focusing on recruitment and onboarding processes.

494
00:24:56,990 --> 00:25:00,030
I'm excited to be here and eager to learn from all of you.

495
00:25:00,030 --> 00:25:05,150
I like that you said, I've just joined. That gives context. Yes, and saying,

496
00:25:05,150 --> 00:25:10,910
eager to learn shows humility and openness. Now let's imagine a more formal scenario.

497
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:13,310
you're meeting a client for the first time.

498
00:25:13,310 --> 00:25:16,310
That requires a slightly more formal tone.

499
00:25:16,310 --> 00:25:18,310
For example, good afternoon,

500
00:25:18,310 --> 00:25:22,510
my name is Speaker 2 and I'm the lead business consultant at our firm.

501
00:25:22,510 --> 00:25:26,510
I specialize in strategic planning and operational efficiency.

502
00:25:26,510 --> 00:25:30,510
It's a pleasure to meet you and we appreciate the opportunity to work together.

503
00:25:30,510 --> 00:25:32,710
That sounds polished and respectful.

504
00:25:32,710 --> 00:25:36,710
Yes, because with clients, professionalism and courtesy are crucial.

505
00:25:36,710 --> 00:25:39,710
I noticed you said, it's a pleasure to meet you.

506
00:25:39,710 --> 00:25:44,990
That's a very useful phrase in business settings. It sounds warm, but still professional.

507
00:25:44,990 --> 00:25:50,590
Let's talk about virtual meetings. Many professionals struggle with introductions on video calls.

508
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:56,350
Yes, especially when there are many participants. What should you include in a virtual introduction?

509
00:25:56,350 --> 00:26:00,750
It's helpful to mention your location if the team is international. For example,

510
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:06,350
Hi everyone, I'm Speaker 2, joining from our Singapore office. I work as a data analyst

511
00:26:06,350 --> 00:26:11,310
in the strategy team. I'll be supporting the analytics for this project. That's very clear

512
00:26:11,310 --> 00:26:17,230
and efficient. Yes, and remember to speak clearly because audio quality may not always be perfect.

513
00:26:17,230 --> 00:26:23,790
Good point. Now let's discuss tone. How do you sound confidence without sounding arrogant?

514
